# pytrees

Python port of the [TREES toolbox](https://www.treestoolbox.org/) — reconstruction,
editing, visualization, analysis and synthesis of neuronal trees.

This is a work in progress. See [PORT_PLAN.md](PORT_PLAN.md) for the porting approach
and [PORT_STATUS.md](PORT_STATUS.md) for the current status of every phase/function.

## Development setup

Recommended: create an isolated environment first (conda or venv) — nothing
in this repo does that for you, and installing straight into a global/base
Python is easy to regret later.

```bash
cd python_port
conda create -n pytrees python=3.11 -y   # or: python -m venv .venv
conda activate pytrees                   # or: .venv\Scripts\activate (Windows) / source .venv/bin/activate

pip install -e ".[dev]"       # core + pytest
pip install -e ".[plot,dev]"  # + pyvista/matplotlib, for plotting.py and examples/
# or: pip install -r requirements.txt   (pinned to known-working versions)

pytest
```
